## Purpose

Step 1 of the parser-owned output grammar work for the Rust frontend: introduce the interfaces and the request lifecycle that let an *initialized* parser build the structured-output grammar for a request, while keeping every path on today's grammar. **This PR is a pure refactor: no request lowers differently than before**, except for the two edge cases called out at the bottom.

Today the strict-tool-calling structural tag is built inside `DefaultChatOutputProcessor::new`, before the prompt is rendered and tokenized, from a `StructuralTagBuilder` the parser merely exposes. The parser itself learns its start state only when the stream's `Start` event arrives (`UnifiedParser::initialize(prompt_token_ids)`), after the grammar has been fixed. Follow-ups (reasoning-phase wrappers, the Kimi K3 native builder) need the grammar to be derived from the initialized parser, so the grammar has to move after tokenization.

### Interface changes

Parser crate (`vllm-parser`), new module `output_grammar`. `UnifiedParser::structural_tag_builder()` is removed; `ToolParser::structural_tag_builder()` stays only as the target of the default forwarder and is documented as to-be-deprecated.

```rust
/// How much of the generated stream the grammar covers.
pub enum GrammarCoverage {
    /// The grammar encodes reasoning and its transition; the engine masks and
    /// advances from the first generated token (`reasoning_ended = Some(true)`).
    FromTokenZero,
    /// The grammar describes only the post-reasoning output; the engine's
    /// reasoning gate decides when it activates (`reasoning_ended = None`).
    FinalOutputOnly,
}

pub struct BuiltOutputGrammar {
    pub format: Format,
    pub coverage: GrammarCoverage,
}

pub struct OutputGrammarContext<'a> {
    pub tools: &'a [Tool],
    pub tool_choice: &'a ToolChoice,
    pub tool_strict_level: ToolStrictLevel,
}

pub trait ToolParser: Send {
    /// Language of everything the model may emit after reasoning ends:
    /// visible text plus tool calls. `None` means no tool grammar applies.
    /// Default: today's gating, then `structural_tag_builder()` with reasoning=false.
    fn build_visible_format(&self, ctx: &OutputGrammarContext<'_>) -> Result<Option<Format>>;
}

pub trait ReasoningParser: Send {
    /// Prepend the reasoning phase implied by the initialized state.
    /// `None` means this parser does not yet own the reasoning phase. Default: `None`.
    fn wrap_visible_format(&self, ctx: &OutputGrammarContext<'_>, visible: &Format) -> Result<Option<Format>>;
}

pub trait UnifiedParser: Send {
    /// Called after `initialize()` and before any generated delta.
    /// `CombinedParser`: tool builds the visible language, reasoning optionally
    /// wraps it; a wrap yields `FromTokenZero`, otherwise `FinalOutputOnly`.
    /// Kimi K3 and HY v3/v4 forward to their crate builder as `FinalOutputOnly`.
    fn build_output_grammar(&self, ctx: &OutputGrammarContext<'_>) -> Result<Option<BuiltOutputGrammar>>;
}
```

Chat crate (`vllm-chat`). The processor is still constructed before rendering, as today; two phases are added once the final prompt token IDs are known.

```rust
pub trait ChatOutputProcessor: Send {
    /// Initialize request-scoped parser state from the final prompt token IDs.
    /// Replaces the initialization previously done on the stream `Start` event.
    fn initialize(&mut self, prompt_token_ids: &[u32]) -> Result<()> { Ok(()) }
    /// Grammar implied by the initialized parser state; `None` if no
    /// parser-owned grammar applies. Harmony keeps the default.
    fn build_output_grammar(&self) -> Result<Option<BuiltOutputGrammar>> { Ok(None) }
    fn process(self: Box<Self>, decoded: DynDecodedTextEventStream) -> Result<DynChatEventStream>;
}

impl ChatRequestProcessor {
    /// resolve parser -> render -> tokenize_in_place -> initialize
    /// -> build_output_grammar -> apply onto TextRequest (structured_outputs,
    /// reasoning_ended). A parser-owned grammar still replaces a user
    /// constraint, as today. `ChatRequest` is never written to.
    pub async fn prepare(&self, request: ChatRequest, text: &TextRequestProcessor)
        -> Result<(TextRequest, DynChatOutputProcessor)>;
}
```

Text crate (`vllm-text`) and lowering.

```rust
impl TextRequestProcessor {
    /// Tokenize and truncate in place, consuming `prompt_truncation`, so the
    /// later `prepare` inside `TextLlm::generate` reuses the token IDs.
    pub fn tokenize_in_place(&self, request: &mut TextRequest) -> Result<&[u32]>;
}

pub struct TextRequest {
    /// Always filled by chat from the effective template kwargs and always
    /// forwarded; the engine reads it only when it owns grammar activation.
    pub reasoning_parser_kwargs: ReasoningParserKwargs, // was Option
    /// Lowered straight through to `EngineCoreRequest.reasoning_ended`
    /// (previously hard-coded `None`). `None` for every path in this PR.
    pub reasoning_ended: Option<bool>,
}
```

### Behavior

- Preserve grammar JSON and `--tool-strict-level` behavior: required/named choices activate tool constraints; `auto` activates with a strict tool or the `function`/`parameter` floor. The `parameter` floor enforces every argument schema, and omitted per-tool `strict` resolves to false. `ToolStrictLevel` and its parsing/display implementations move into `vllm_parser::output_grammar`, retaining the public chat re-export; `GrammarInputs` forwards the policy through `OutputGrammarContext`.
- `reasoning_ended` is `None` for every request, exactly as before; no reasoning parser overrides `wrap_visible_format` yet, so `FromTokenZero` is unreachable in this PR.
- Two deliberate edge-case changes, both outside the main path:
  - A failing `UnifiedParser::initialize` now rejects the request before submission (`OutputParserInitialization`) instead of logging a warning mid-stream and degrading to plain-text deltas. The fallback only existed because initialization happened where rejection was impossible.
  - Completions and gRPC requests now send an empty `reasoning_parser_kwargs` (`{chat_template_kwargs: {}}`) instead of `null`. The engine reads it only when constructing a reasoner for a structured-output request, which those paths never have.

## Test Plan

```bash
cd rust
cargo nextest run -p vllm-parser -p vllm-chat --lib --all-features --locked
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings
```

Existing HY v3/v4 structural-tag tests now go through `build_output_grammar` and assert `FinalOutputOnly`; `output_grammar::tests` covers activation and strictness resolution; `output_grammar_preserves_tool_strict_level` covers forwarding from chat to the parser; `output::structural_tag::tests` covers grammar application onto `TextRequest`. Roundtrip tests (need model files) call `initialize` explicitly before `process`.

## Test Result

- After rebasing onto `dbf4b89cf2` (including #57272), Step 1's parser/chat unit tests: **800 passed, 0 skipped**.
- `cargo check -p vllm-chat --all-targets` passed.
- Full workspace Clippy with all targets/features and warnings denied, formatting, and pre-commit passed on the rebased stack.
- On the complete rebased Step 1/2 stack, parser/chat/text tests: **940 passed, 1 skipped**, including renderer/parser roundtrips and the real-Qwen generation-default test.

